    <h2>Keeping a Big Table Moving</h2>
    <p>The enemy of a 20-player game is dead time, so the host has tools to keep it brisk. Set a shorter turn timer (15–30 seconds works well for big groups) so nobody stalls the table, and auto-play will take a reasonable turn for anyone who steps away. Latecomers can join as spectators and drop into the next round, and if someone's connection drops, they reconnect straight back into their seat with their hand intact. As host you can also kick an idle player, reorder seats, and pick the <a href="/game-modes">game mode</a> before you start.</p>

    <h2>Works Everywhere, for Everyone</h2>
    <p>Every player joins from their own device — phone, tablet, laptop, or desktop — with no installs and no accounts. Just share the room code or invite link and everyone is in the game within seconds. The interface scales cleanly whether there are 3 players or 20, so a huge table stays just as easy to read as a small one.</p>

